From: WG2600HP isolated staging audit (2026-11-01)
Subject: [CANDIDATE 760-07] select QCA 802.1Q on both DSA CPU ports

NOT FOR BUILD OR DEPLOYMENT. Depends on complete and verified
760-01 tagger, 760-02 QCA8K switch integration, 760-03 dual-CPU
isolation, 760-06 error cleanup, and pinned ECM 760-04/05.
Default Linux v6.12.112 dsa.c reads the "dsa-tag-protocol" DT
property from each CPU port; both CPU ports in one switch tree must
select the same protocol. Kconfig must also build the new tagger.
No user-facing VLAN interfaces or board network settings are added.
Do not merge until G1/G2 proof and rollback safety are complete.

---
--- a/target/linux/ipq806x/config-6.12
+++ b/target/linux/ipq806x/config-6.12
@@ -331,6 +331,7 @@
 CONFIG_NET_DSA_QCA8K=y
 CONFIG_NET_DSA_QCA8K_LEDS_SUPPORT=y
 CONFIG_NET_DSA_TAG_QCA=y
+CONFIG_NET_DSA_TAG_QCA_8021Q=y
 CONFIG_NET_EGRESS=y
 CONFIG_NET_FLOW_LIMIT=y
 CONFIG_NET_INGRESS=y
--- a/target/linux/ipq806x/files-6.12/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-ipq8064-wg2600hp.dts
+++ b/target/linux/ipq806x/files-6.12/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-ipq8064-wg2600hp.dts
@@ -158,6 +158,7 @@
 				reg = <0>;
 				label = "cpu";
 				ethernet = <&gmac1>;
+				dsa-tag-protocol = "qca-8021q";
 				phy-mode = "rgmii";
 				tx-internal-delay-ps = <1000>;
 
@@ -206,6 +207,7 @@
 				reg = <6>;
 				label = "cpu";
 				ethernet = <&gmac2>;
+				dsa-tag-protocol = "qca-8021q";
 				phy-mode = "sgmii";
 				qca,sgmii-enable-pll;
 				qca,sgmii-rxclk-falling-edge;
